cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tessera: every person a tile; together they show the pattern"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roy
    given-names: Abhik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7085-8964"
repository-code: "https://github.com/drabhikroy/tessera"
abstract: >-
  An open source R Shiny application for social network analysis.
  Classical, transparent graph methods turn a list of ties between people
  into an interactive map, with plain language readings for general users
  and full statistics for researchers, including extended centralities,
  a choice of community detection algorithms, global diagnostics, and the
  dyad and triad census. An optional language model running on the same
  machine adds interpretation without changing any number.
keywords:
  - social network analysis
  - graph theory
  - community detection
  - centrality
  - R
  - Shiny
  - program evaluation
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: 0.13.0
date-released: "2026-07-23"
